= The Debt Ceiling

The new House majority demands cuts in exchange for raising the debt ceiling. The Treasury warns of default. The Constitution says the debt must be paid.

- @negotiate: Negotiate a deal.
- @stand: Refuse to negotiate.

@negotiate
subtitle: Pragmatic.
on-arrival: stability += 2; prog_dissent += 3; mod_dissent -= 2; pop_mod += 0.1

A compromise passes, with some cuts and a suspension of the ceiling.

@stand
subtitle: Principle, risk.
on-arrival: stability -= 2; enthusiasm += 2; prog_dissent -= 2; mod_dissent += 1

The standoff stretches to the last minute.
